{"kind":"request","text":"Concrete replay-budget disposition for the ordered fixed-slot index request. Ruling 74286ee7 confirms verify --all must report every scope consistent in the actual 2,000-member room.\n\nSource at Main 909d8a1a3b9ada6dd1bed9c49511a479a2428ea6: add-member emits a real Inbox create (packages/platform/src/membership.ts). verify --all follows every actual create seed, without an Inbox/owner filter (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:835–865), and the real admin Membership session can read those full journals. replayOf creates a separate replay verifier for each target (commands.ts:751–802,885–888); every Inbox proves its Membership creation prefix again (packages/replay/src/verify.ts:1119–1157,1606–1611). Even one Membership entry per addition gives sum(1..2000) = 2,001,000 prefix entries before other work, above the shared default 100,000 received-entry bound (packages/cli/src/verification.ts:14). This is source-derived work, not a measured run or claim about final timing.\n\nThe maintained Context.verify port supports explicit finite limits. Please decide whether the acceptance witness may invoke the same verify --all command against the real native room with an explicitly recorded, finite caller budget, while preserving shipped defaults and making no default-CLI completion claim. The concrete bound would be derived and retained with the witness, not silently treated as unlimited.\n\nIf the intended acceptance is the unmodified default command budget, please file and order a bounded CLI proof-reuse child before that replay acceptance. Do not solve this by suppressing Inbox creation, omitting scopes, inventing anchors, or silently raising production defaults. Index/kernel preparation remains read-only and unclaimed until c303 lands; its current exact-head review is active.","body":{"conditions":"Decide whether the 2,000-member verify --all witness may use explicit finite Context.verify limits, with shipped defaults unchanged and that boundary reported, or whether a separately scoped CLI proof-reuse improvement must precede its acceptance. State the intended witness boundary; no implementation artifact or new default limit is requested by this question.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}